## Agent Management

### Available Operations

- `list`: Get all agents (returns id, name, description)
- `read`: Get full agent configuration (`agent_id` required - numeric)
- `create`: Create new agent
- `update`: Modify agent (`agent_id` required)
- `delete`: Delete agent (`agent_id` required)

### Agent Structure

```json
{
  "id": 15,
  "name": "Customer Support Agent",
  "description": "Handles customer inquiries",
  "instructions": "You are a helpful customer support agent...",
  "skills": [42, 43, 44],
  "tools": ["gmail-send-email", "slack-send-message"],
  "model": "gpt-4o",
  "team_id": 1
}
```

### Creating an Agent

Required fields:
- `name`: Agent display name
- `description`: What the agent does

Optional fields:
- `instructions`: Custom system prompt
- `skills`: Array of skill IDs to enable
- `tools`: Array of tool names to enable
- `model`: Model override (defaults to org setting)
- `team_id`: Team assignment

### Example: Create Support Agent

```
1. List available skills:
   skill_crud(method="list")

2. Create agent with skills:
   agent_crud(method="create",
              name="Support Agent",
              description="Handles support tickets",
              skills=[42, 43],
              tools=["gmail-send-email"])
```

### Updating Agents

When updating, provide only the fields you want to change:
```
agent_crud(method="update", agent_id=15,
           instructions="Updated instructions...")
```

For arrays (skills, tools), provide the COMPLETE updated array.

### Important Notes

- Agent IDs are numeric
- Skill IDs in the `skills` array must be numeric
- Tool names must match available tool names exactly
- Agents inherit org-level model if not specified
